{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Information.DimqRegularisationIdentities","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Information.DimqRegularisationIdentities","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.LinearCombination","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.DimqRegularisation.qint_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.DimqRegularisation.qint_two","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/DimqRegularisationIdentities.lean#L74-L83","doc":"`[2]_q = (q² − q⁻²)/(q − q⁻¹) = q + q⁻¹` — the quantum dimension of the\nfundamental object, finite for every `q ≠ 0` with `q² ≠ 1` (equivalently\n`q − q⁻¹ ≠ 0`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.DimqRegularisation.hadamard_eq_neg_six_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.DimqRegularisation.hadamard_eq_neg_six_iff","kind":"theorem","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/DimqRegularisationIdentities.lean#L60-L72","doc":"The Hadamard finite part `−1/u²` equals `−6` iff `u² = 1/6`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.DimqRegularisation.zeta_numerator_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.DimqRegularisation.zeta_numerator_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/DimqRegularisationIdentities.lean#L52-L58","doc":"Hence the ζ-regularised numerator `(−1) − 2·ζ(0)` vanishes once `ζ(0)` is\ntaken as `−1/2`: the scheme gives `dim_q^ζ(A) = 0` for every admissible `q`.\n(`CharZero` is needed only to know that `2 ≠ 0`.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.DimqRegularisation.zeta_geometric_pair_eq_neg_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.DimqRegularisation.zeta_geometric_pair_eq_neg_one","kind":"theorem","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/DimqRegularisationIdentities.lean#L37-L50","doc":"The two continued geometric series sum to `−1`:\n`q²/(1 − q²) + q⁻²/(1 − q⁻²) = −1` whenever `q ≠ 0` and `q² ≠ 1`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}